  "bio": [
    "Kuldip Rathee chairs and runs New Delhi-based ASK Automotive, a manufacturer of auto components such as brakes for two-wheelers.",
    "ASK Automotive  also makes brake disc pads and assemblies as well as safety control cables for speedometers and clutch assemblies.",
    "Its list of clients includes TVS Motor Company, Hero MotoCorp, Suzuki, Yamaha and Royal Enfield.",
    "It has 18 factories located across six Indian states.",
    "His wife Vijay and sons Aman and Prashant sit on the company's board."
  ],
  "about": [
    "He has a B.A. in economics from St. Stephen's College in Delhi.",
    "In the 1970s he worked as a police officer for the Central Reserve Police Force, which is a federal body."
  ]
